 r←GetDocsUrl path;name;base;old;new;ind
⍝ Takes the path of a page from the documentation Tatin used to serve itself, such as
⍝ "/docs/FirstStepsWithTatin.html", and returns the URL of whatever replaced it.
⍝ Where nothing corresponds - a page that was dropped rather than rewritten - the index of
⍝ the documentation is returned. A reader who lands there is one click from what they wanted;
⍝ one who lands on a 404 is gone.
⍝ The name is folded to lower case before it is looked up because these files were named in
⍝ CamelCase for some years and in lower case afterwards, and links to both are still about.
 base←'https://aplteam.github.io/Tatin/'
 old←'firststepswithtatin' 'initializingtatin' 'introduction' 'caching'
 new←'get-started' 'get-started' '' ''
 old,←'installingandupdatingthetatinclient' 'installingthetatinserver' 'packageconfiguration'
 new,←'install-tatin' 'install-server' 'package-configuration'
 old,←'publishingpackages' 'rundyalogbehindapache' 'semanticversioning' 'syntaxreference'
 new,←'publish-packages' 'secure-server' 'semantic-versioning' 'user-commands'
 old,←'tatinforcontributors' 'fordevelopers' 'tatinusersettings' 'usersettings'
 new,←'contribute' 'develop' 'user-settings' 'user-settings'
 old,←'tatinsloadandupdatestrategy' 'tatinsupdatestrategy' 'servermaintenance' 'server-tipsandtricks'
 new,←'load-and-update-strategy' 'load-and-update-strategy' 'maintenance' 'maintenance'
 old,←'github' 'releasenotes' 'usagedata' 'tatinandonedrive'
 new,←'github-rate-limits' 'release-notes' 'host' ''
 old,←'managing_packages_with_tatin' 'tatin_spec' '_readme'
 new,←'' '' ''
 name←⊃⌽'/'A.Split path                             ⍝ The last segment, so any folder in between is ignored
 name←⎕C{⍵↑⍨¯1+⍵⍳'.'}name                           ⍝ ... without its extension
 r←base
 :If (≢old)≥ind←old⍳⊂name
 :AndIf 0<≢ind⊃new
     r←base,(ind⊃new),'/'
 :EndIf
⍝Done
